        <div class="hopt-tradeoffs">
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Pros</h3>
            <p>Full cinematic bleed while you read. Header is available on first paint (no discoverability hit)
            and reappears as soon as you scroll up. Best of both worlds for media-heavy heroes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Cons</h3>
            <p>Requires a scroll-direction script; a tiny bit of layout choreography. On very short pages or
            in iframes (Embeds, GitHub Pages preview) the hide/show is less useful. Some users prefer always-visible nav.</p>
