            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hopt-tradeoffs">
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Pros</h3>
            <p>Full cinematic bleed. Top of the meaningful video frame is never hidden — the header sits over
            the natural sky/empty zone the shot already has. No re-encode, no extension assets, no scroll
            choreography. Works for every existing hero video so long as content isn't anchored to the top edge.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Cons</h3>
            <p>Depends on the video composition having sky / empty space at the top. If a hero ever needs
            content right at the top edge (e.g. a sun framed at 5% from top), it gets pushed off-screen. Mitigation:
            re-encode that specific video with a top extension (mirrored-blurred sky) and reuse the same layout.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hopt-approve-row"><a href="mailto:svge.india@gmail.com?subject=Approve%20Hero%20Option%2005" class="hopt-approve">Approve Option 05</a></div>
