            <div class="hopt-copy">
              <p class="eyebrow">{eyebrow}</p>
              <p class="mock-h1">{h1Top} <span class="accent">{h1Mid}</span> {h1Bottom}</p>
              <p class="sub">{sub}</p>
              <div class="hopt-ctas">
                <a href="#" class="hopt-cta primary">Talk to us →</a>
                <a href="#" class="hopt-cta ghost">See the project →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hopt-tradeoffs">
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Pros</h3>
            <p>Most defensive. Header sits entirely above the original frame — zero risk of cropping meaningful
            content, regardless of how a future video is composed. The extension is mirrored-blurred from the
            video's own top pixels so it feels native, not stamped-on. Layout still reads as full-bleed cinema.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="hopt-tradeoff">
            <h3>Cons</h3>
            <p>Requires a one-time re-encode per hero video (already done for all 5: home, about, farmers, impact,
            process). Video aspect changes from 16:9 to 1280:840 (~3:2). On widescreen viewports the video may
            crop slightly on sides if hero is height-constrained — adjust with <code>object-position</code> if needed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hopt-approve-row"><a href="mailto:svge.india@gmail.com?subject=Approve%20Hero%20Option%2006" class="hopt-approve">Approve Option 06</a></div>
